course: dictionary
lesson: 5086
title: Integrity: honest and whole
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Integrity is a noun. It names a quality, the kind of person you are when you do the right thing. It has two main meanings: being honest and doing what is right even when nobody is watching, and being whole and strong, not broken.
explain: «Telling a teacher about a mistake that gave you a better mark shows real integrity.» Nobody would ever find out if you kept quiet, so telling the teacher is the honest and right thing to do. The clue is in the sentence: honesty when no one would know means integrity.
explain: «The integrity of the bridge» uses the second meaning. The bridge is whole and strong, with no cracks or breaks. Engineers call this structural integrity. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence, then check it by putting your meaning into the sentence.
fact: Integrity is a noun, and it is uncountable, so say «real integrity», not «a real integrity».
fact: «Integrity» means being honest and doing what is right, even when nobody is watching.
fact: «Integrity» can also mean being whole and strong, not broken, as in «the integrity of the bridge».
fact: Useful phrases include «a person of integrity», «show integrity» and «academic integrity».
fact: Academic integrity means being honest in your schoolwork, such as not cheating and telling the truth when it is hard.
exercise: «Telling a teacher about a mistake that gave you a better mark shows real integrity.» What does integrity mean here? | Being quick and clever at sums | Being whole and strong like a bridge | Being loud and confident in class | *Being honest and doing what is right, even when nobody is watching
exercise: «Telling the teacher about a marking mistake in your favour shows integrity.» Find and copy the words that tell you the mistake helped you. | marking mistake | shows integrity | the teacher | *in your favour
exercise: «Engineers checked the integrity of the bridge before the cars drove over it.» What does integrity mean in this sentence? | *Being whole and strong, with no cracks or breaks | Being very tall and high | Being honest with the engineers | Being painted in bright colours
test: «If a teacher adds up your marks wrongly in your favour, telling them is real integrity.» Why is telling the teacher integrity, and not just a nice thing to do? | Because it makes the lesson finish early | *Because you are being honest even when nobody would find out | Because you will get a bigger mark next time | Because the teacher will give you a sticker
test: «Structural integrity» is a phrase used in science and building. What does it describe? | *A structure that is strong and safe | A plant that grows quickly | A person who always tells the truth | A test you take at the end of term
exam: «A person of integrity keeps their promises and does not cheat.» What does «a person of integrity» mean? | Someone who is always first in the queue | *Someone who is honest and does what is right | Someone who has a large collection of coins | Someone who never speaks in class
